{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/488921-i-need-to-get-up-to-speed","id":488921,"title":"\"I need to get up to speed.\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-22T18:45:23-07:00","id":488921,"title":"\"I need to get up to speed.\"","content":"One of my characters was born in 1970, abducted in 1985, and spent twenty years (her time) playing through expanded-setting versions of the laserdisc games popular at the time: Road Blasters, Cobra Command, Thayer's Quest, Time Gal, Badlands, Cliff Hanger, Space Ace, Braindead 13, Freedom Fighter, Space Ace, and of course both Dragon's Lair games. After completing all of them in a single marathon run, she's driven herself out of the Hedge in Lance's van from Braindead 13. She's fit, strong, agile, with a vast array of (mostly combat related) skills, a small armoury of Tokens... and it's now 2015 and she hasn't aged a day, physically. Which aspects of modern life will most take her aback? One obvious question will be &quot;since when did pagers become fashion accessories?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:54:13-07:00","id":489001,"title":"","content":"Well an easy answer will of course be the internet and the way it has changed knowledge. Before if you wanted to know something you went to a library and searched. You could go years wondering about something and never know the answer. Now you can have answers within seconds. Interestingly I read a paper recently that indicates we may be getting <i>dumber </i>from this, as we no longer form solid memories about knowledge since it is so easily accessible, and most people really do take what they find on the net at face value. The output is that while we think we are much more knowledgeable, we are in fact far less. We may know some bullet points about something, but we generally don't <i>understand </i>the topic because that requires true investigation and reading.<br /> <br /> The other thing (which bothers me irl) is the level of intrusion of social media and technology in our lives. Twitter, Facebook. Realizing the you can actually track when someone is taking a shit from anywhere on the planet. Probably major culture shock. I could see that spawning some serious paranoia. I mean your character basically just came from 1984, and now they are living in the Orwell book.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just some random blathering. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T21:07:09-07:00","id":489004,"title":"","content":"Internet culture. Everybody's got smartphones with wi-fi access, checking Youtube on the go. The smartphones have cameras, and random bystanders can record a video of something unexpected and have it blow up across the news worldwide within a day or two. If she gets into a street fight she might have to check to make sure it doesn't show up on Worldstar. Information is pervasive and invasive. No one is anonymous. Strangers are closer than ever, but the people right next to you feel less intimate.<br /> <br /> Global insurgency. She never lived through the 9/11 terrorist attacks or the ensuing international effects of America's military response. Airport security is suddenly very strangely selective, often settling into laxity and boredom, but bursting into severity under certain triggers. The spread of information and travel has ensured that the world must be mindful of the politics of regions halfway around the world, because their repercussions can potentially reach anywhere. The notion of military action is immediate and personal in a way that it hasn't been for Americans since the Vietnam War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}